    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Electron arrangement",
     "md": "Electrons fill shells from the nucleus outwards: **first shell 2, second 8, third 8** (for the first 20 elements), then the fourth shell. Sodium (Z = 11): **2, 8, 1**; chlorine (Z = 17): **2, 8, 7**; calcium (Z = 20): **2, 8, 8, 2**. The number of outer-shell electrons is the **group number**; the number of occupied shells is the **period**. An atom with a full outer shell (helium 2, neon 2,8, argon 2,8,8) is **unreactive**."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Isotopes",
     "md": "**Isotopes** are atoms of the same element (same Z) with **different numbers of neutrons** (different A). They have the **same chemical properties** because they have the same electrons. Examples: carbon-12 and carbon-14; chlorine-35 and chlorine-37. The **relative atomic mass A_r** is the average mass of the atoms of an element compared with 1/12 of an atom of carbon-12: chlorine is about 35.5 because natural chlorine is about 75 % Cl-35 and 25 % Cl-37."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Isotopes have the same number of **protons**, not the same number of neutrons.\n- The mass number is not the atomic number: Na has Z = 11 and A = 23.\n- The second shell holds 8 electrons, not 2: only the first shell holds 2."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Particles in an atom",
     "statement": "Sodium has atomic number 11 and mass number 23. Give the number of protons, neutrons and electrons and the electron arrangement.",
     "steps": [
      "Protons = Z = 11; electrons = 11; neutrons = 23 − 11 = 12.",
      "Electrons fill 2, 8 and then 1 in the third shell: 2, 8, 1."
     ],
     "answer": "11 protons, 12 neutrons, 11 electrons; 2, 8, 1"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Average mass of chlorine",
     "statement": "Chlorine is 75 % Cl-35 and 25 % Cl-37. Find its relative atomic mass.",
     "steps": [
      "Average = 0.75 × 35 + 0.25 × 37.",
      "= 26.25 + 9.25 = 35.5."
     ],
     "answer": "35.5"
    },
