    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Groups and periods",
     "md": "The periodic table arranges elements in order of **atomic number**. A vertical column is a **group**: elements in a group have the **same number of outer electrons** and similar properties. A horizontal row is a **period**: it shows the number of **shells**. Across a period there is a change from **metals** (left) to **non-metals** (right), ending in a noble gas."
    },
